<%# THE STIMULUS SCOPE, and what it is deliberately NOT attached to.

    `#turn_log` is replaced by a Turbo Stream at the end of every turn, so a
    controller there would be disconnected and reconnected constantly -- and the
    one thing this controller must survive is exactly that replacement, since
    hooking the stream render is its whole job. So the scope is this wrapper,
    which nothing replaces and which exists only to be it.

    Not `<body>` either: the layout is shared with the index, and there is no
    narration to follow there.

    `@window` / `@document` on the actions because neither event reaches this
    element on its own. Page `scroll` fires on `window`, and
    `turbo:before-stream-render` is dispatched by the `<turbo-stream>` element
    Turbo appends to `document.documentElement` -- outside this subtree, so it
    never bubbles through here. Stimulus adds and removes both listeners with
    the element, which is what it buys us over two bare `addEventListener`
    calls that nothing ever took back. %>
<div data-controller="play"
     data-action="scroll@window->play#notePosition
                  turbo:load@document->play#notePosition
                  turbo:before-stream-render@document->play#followStreamRender">
  <h1><%= @playthrough.story.title %></h1>
  <%# The window into the machine, and the only mark it leaves on the game.
      Absent entirely unless `Playthrough::Debug.enabled?` -- local by default --
      so a player who was handed a playthrough link is never shown one. %>
  <p>
    <%= link_to "&larr; all stories".html_safe, root_path %>
    <% if Playthrough::Debug.enabled? %>
      &middot; <%= link_to "debug", playthrough_debug_path(@playthrough) %>
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <div class="preface"><%= @playthrough.story.preface %></div>
  <hr>

  <%# THE CABLE. Everything a turn changes is broadcast onto this playthrough's
      stream by NarrationJob: batched chunks of prose while it narrates, then the
      finished `#turn_log` when it lands. Outside `#turn_log` on purpose -- a
      subscription element inside the element being replaced would be torn down
      and rebuilt on every turn, and the tail of the turn would go to a channel
      nobody was listening on yet. %>
  <%= turbo_stream_from @playthrough %>

  <%# `autofocus` here and nowhere else: this is the one render that is a page
      load, so the attribute means what it says. See the note in the partial for
      why a broadcast must not carry it. %>
  <%= render "playthroughs/turn_log", playthrough: @playthrough, command: nil,
                                      autofocus: true %>

  <%# Where the player left off. A plain reload and the index's Resume link both
      aim at `#bottom`, so the browser puts the newest turn on screen with no
      script involved. A brand new playthrough is the deliberate exception:
      PlaythroughsController#create sends the player to the top, where the preface
      and the opening arrival are.

      Taking a turn no longer arrives here at all -- there is no redirect left to
      carry an anchor -- so where the viewport sits while prose arrives is the
      play controller's job, and it follows the narration down only while the
      player is already reading the bottom. %>
  <div id="bottom"></div>
</div>
